@Shreyasg13 Thanks for pointing out the schema-dependent behavior. `288f5b0c2` preserves comma-separated array values as lists when `arg_type == "array"`, while untyped and numeric tuple expressions retain their original text.

The regression coverage now checks numeric and array schemas through serialized GLM-4 tool calls as well as bare comma expressions, string elements, a trailing comma, and explicit tuple literals. The added cases produce five failures at the previous PR head; the complete registered function-call parser file now passes all 253 tests. Applicable pre-commit checks pass too.

This PR continues to touch only `glm4_moe_detector.py`; your GLM-4.7/5 fix in #43270 remains separate.

@Shreyasg13 Thanks for confirming the updated behavior and consistency with #43270.

@JustinTong0323 Could you review this parser fix and start CI for `288f5b0` with `/tag-and-rerun-ci`? I checked all 16 failed jobs: the 10 gates report `Missing required label 'run-ci'`, and the 6 finish jobs fail because those gates failed. The dependent tests were skipped; these runs have not validated the patch. [Base CI gate log](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38013695579/job/114099288910).

The registered parser file passed all 253 tests locally in the previous validation of this same commit. My account has no permission to add the required label. If the Extra workflows are needed, `/tag-and-rerun-ci extra` also adds their `run-ci-extra` opt-in label.

